{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 85, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 85, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=86&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=84&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 469594197, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r469594197-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Really special atmosphere at and around the temple ", "text": "The atmosphere is completely different to the other temples I have visited. The area is large. Entry around 10 usd. It's on the riverside and has a special atmosphere because of the funeral ceremonies. You can only enter the temple if you are hindu. It's a really impressive place that you have to see and feel. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "FAB839218BB47CB4A2A37640FFA4A87F", "name": "Basketforme", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Basketforme", "username": "Basketforme", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f2/59/default-avatar-2020-24.jpg", "contribution_count": 13, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-23", "published_at_date": "2017-03-24"}, {"review_id": 469541019, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r469541019-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Place of Lord Shiva", "text": "We started our Nepal trip after paying visit here. It is a ancient temple of lord Shiva. In the holy place you see a huge statue made of bronze.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2016-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "DE31EB925CCFDFE0798D47EACA47874A", "name": "Yash R", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/436yashr", "username": "436yashr", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/09/50/4b/d0/yash-r.jpg", "contribution_count": 33, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-23", "published_at_date": "2017-03-23"}, {"review_id": 469529639, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r469529639-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "History of when GODS roamed HEAVEN ON EARTH", "text": "For any traveler I guess  visiting places has to be meaningful. Not only wanting to see how wonderful the place is but the history behind it gives us an idea about how civilized and amazing the place was in the past. PASHUPATINATH TEMPLE and its surrounding has been and still a heaven for anybody. The architecture, the monuments, the buildings and moreover the religious value adds to why 1000s of people visit this place everyday. Just to be in the vicinity gives you the tranquil feeling. Sitting by the holy river Bagmati and staring directly at the temple is just breathtaking. Take a walk around the area and one shall immediately find themselves at peace with their inner self. There is so much to do once you get here. If you are in KATHMANDU please take your time to visit this place. Look aside the chaos and the eerie cry of the families of the deceased, by the Holy Bagmati there is more to it. Even the dead find themselves at peace when they come here so imagine what a living human being could seek within.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2017-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "A66C0D49642C0190459EB23BF3789C9B", "name": "Niranjan L", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/841niranjanl", "username": "841niranjanl", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/d2/d9/04/niranjan-l.jpg", "contribution_count": 77, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/bc/ee/a4/view-from-across-the.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-03-23", "published_at_date": "2017-03-23"}, {"review_id": 469502772, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r469502772-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Awkward and strange", "text": "As a non Hindu, I did not find this place appealing or interesting.  Even as a western Hindu, you will not be allowed into the main temple.  Instead, for a $10 you can watch cremation from across the holy Bagmati River, a river so polluted I do not understand how it can be considered holy and treated with such broad civil irreverence.  I would not visit here again.\n\n", "review_tip": null, "rating": 1, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C2D4B4486FFFA30C314F4705251CB12F", "name": "Nick R", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/461nickr", "username": "461nickr", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/08/7d/b3/15/nick-r.jpg", "contribution_count": 168, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-23", "published_at_date": "2017-03-23"}, {"review_id": 469486081, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r469486081-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Interesting to see", "text": "it is interesting to visit and see how other religions deal with death. you will hear a lot of crying and screaming but it is normal for burial procedures. this probably will make you sad. do not stand in the smoke as it comes from the burning of a dead body and it smells bad", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2016-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "736F28764C46A3A5038A8337F477ECB1", "name": "bio791", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/bio791", "username": "bio791", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-f/01/2e/70/67/avatar045.jpg", "contribution_count": 104, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 189417, "location_name": "Heraklion", "location_name_detailed": "Heraklion, Greece"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-22", "published_at_date": "2017-03-23"}, {"review_id": 469366022, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r469366022-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Great Hindu temple", "text": "Pashupatinath is one of the great Hindu temple in Nepal. Shiva is main god inside the temple. Its really attraction place to visit.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2016-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "529476B4E6B34848B74216CCF167BE6C", "name": "georgelun10", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/georgelun10", "username": "georgelun10", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f2/eb/default-avatar-2020-27.jpg", "contribution_count": 4, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255068, "location_name": "Brisbane", "location_name_detailed": "Brisbane, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-22", "published_at_date": "2017-03-23"}, {"review_id": 469342003, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r469342003-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "major Hindu shrine", "text": "Major Hindu Shrine in Kathmandu\nplace of pilgrimage for Hindus from inside and outside Nepal\nplace of cremation\nyou can see the funeral pyres", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2017-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "BA570CE180C9C6014FC05DDF8228249E", "name": "drpaulc69", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/drpaulc69", "username": "drpaulc69", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e9/ef/default-avatar-2020-66.jpg", "contribution_count": 21, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255060, "location_name": "Sydney", "location_name_detailed": "Sydney, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-22", "published_at_date": "2017-03-23"}, {"review_id": 469147991, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r469147991-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Never seen a funeral pyre before. Very interesting place. Very atmospheric", "text": "This is where many of the people of Kathmandu come to cremate their deceased, and if you stand on the river bank you can see the ceremonies and cremations. A very atmospheric place, well deserving of its world heritage status. Must-see.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "6398DF9377674AEDBA0F20870425CCA0", "name": "Stephen P", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/stephenpZ9823KT", "username": "stephenpZ9823KT", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e8/5b/default-avatar-2020-61.jpg", "contribution_count": 22, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 57353, "location_name": "Norwich", "location_name_detailed": "Norwich, Vermont"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-21", "published_at_date": "2017-03-22"}, {"review_id": 469146010, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r469146010-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "a religious site", "text": "Pashupatinath temple is a Hindu temple. This temple is frequented by the locals and it is most popular. There is a crematorium within this site. They burn dead bodies along the river. It is very interesting to visit here as one can see how the people worship and offer their offerings. There is an entry fee to the temple. This temple is very busy .", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "0AF8347C47EE56693731B34BE707E680", "name": "SHDD", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/SHDD", "username": "SHDD", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/05/53/9e/c5/shdd.jpg", "contribution_count": 1472, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 312578, "location_name": "Johannesburg", "location_name_detailed": "Johannesburg, South Africa"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/b9/cb/0c/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/b9/cb/18/pashupatinath-temple.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/b9/cb/22/pashupatinath-temple.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-03-21", "published_at_date": "2017-03-22"}, {"review_id": 469101570, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r469101570-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Mind blowing!", "text": "went here a while ago. what to say - home of Lord Shiva. went as part of a tour group and was priviledged to perform a havan here. beautiful temple - one of the most revered temples in Hinduism! love it.!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2016-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "11026DC6D142D6D0EAD23BB89F48B265", "name": "Yuvraj21", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Yuvraj21", "username": "Yuvraj21", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e3/6a/default-avatar-2020-47.jpg", "contribution_count": 105, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 186338, "location_name": "London", "location_name_detailed": "London, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-21", "published_at_date": "2017-03-22"}, {"review_id": 469037346, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r469037346-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Witness Human Cremations and Ceremonies", "text": "You may find it unbelievable but this temple is one of Lord Shiva's largest in Nepal and Hindus are cremated almost every day.  We watched two cremations along the river. I do have photos of the corpses but out of respect I will not post them,\nThere is no smell of burning flesh as the body is covered with spices and herbs and this and the charcoal smell are more evident.  Walk around for more than an hour, climb and see views from terraces and give a few rupees to the quiet beggars along the paths.  Only Hindus can go into certain temples. There are numerous opportunities for photos.  Sadhus are willing to allow a photo and none asked for rupees; they simply smiled.  We found this the most interesting place in Kathmandu.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "2300DAB06D3AE6FA143A225DFDF2179D", "name": "Marie M", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/598MarieM", "username": "598MarieM", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/05/4c/13/38/marie-m.jpg", "contribution_count": 607, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293917, "location_name": "Chiang Mai", "location_name_detailed": "Chiang Mai, Thailand"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/b9/06/56/photo0jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-03-21", "published_at_date": "2017-03-21"}, {"review_id": 468556080, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r468556080-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Awesome place", "text": "you should see it! Where they burn their dead bodies... Very imirtant experiance. And beatiful buildings!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "business", "stay_date": "2017-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "1D5358F2AD3010A97FBCF17BCEAF6354", "name": "Jakob B", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/jakobb519", "username": "jakobb519", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e7/7b/default-avatar-2020-56.jpg", "contribution_count": 4, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-19", "published_at_date": "2017-03-20"}, {"review_id": 468496414, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r468496414-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Pilgrimage", "text": "It's one of the best Shiva Temples I have ever visited, very systematic, we paid through shrine bank that gave us satisfaction", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "AFEB13D977AC71C8199652407F3C20E3", "name": "deepakrenu", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/deepakrenu", "username": "deepakrenu", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e4/2d/default-avatar-2020-48.jpg", "contribution_count": 6, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-19", "published_at_date": "2017-03-20"}, {"review_id": 468415911, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r468415911-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Hindu religious site- one of the 12 Jyotirlingas.", "text": "A great Hindu religious site. No 'pandas/priests' to pester you. Only a few steps to climb unlike many Hindu temples. A short walk from the car park. Puja offerings quite straightforward via a short queue. Temple closes at 7 pm. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "75E81B2C45AFEE2D028327B962E957F4", "name": "NarayanMelb", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/NarayanMelb", "username": "NarayanMelb", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f2/b8/default-avatar-2020-26.jpg", "contribution_count": 182, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255100, "location_name": "Melbourne", "location_name_detailed": "Melbourne, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-19", "published_at_date": "2017-03-19"}, {"review_id": 468195175, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r468195175-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "for inner travel", "text": "Pasupathinath temple first appears to be normal when u enter as just an another hindu temple. But the ambience, Pasupathi, bunch of temples, open cremation and the scent in air, baghmathi river, kala bhairava all makes u to travel somewhere inner. U understand or reveal or identify something from that. It is not by bhakthi. So it is still claimed as one of the holy, ancient and main temples of Hindu Religion. Feel it.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2017-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "89C0EF96786CF7780A5BB66503186F30", "name": "nesamoorthy", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/nesamoorthy", "username": "nesamoorthy", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0e/b1/da/4c/nesamoorthy.jpg", "contribution_count": 5, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 297628, "location_name": "Bengaluru", "location_name_detailed": "Bengaluru, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-03-18", "published_at_date": "2017-03-18"}, {"review_id": 468077521, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r468077521-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Awesome temple to visit : shambo pashupatinath", "text": "We visited this temple on 11th March 2017. Its an Awesome temple with unique shivling hosting a huge idol of Nandi in the entrance. Bhagmati river flows behind and makes the temple even more beautiful. Photography is prohibited inside the temple but can take photos before entrance. Shopping around the temple is for reasonable price. Shop owners are eager to accept Indian currency and no need to convert INR to NPR in Nepal. Who ever visits Kathmandu should and must visit this temple. It took 20 min for us to have Lord Shiva's Darshan. It takes around 2 to 4 hrs for over all visit depending on the rush at the temple. As the photography is prohibited inside the temple i am uploading the photos taken outside in front of the entrance", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "5FA02B09B81524BC15C3E592209508DF", "name": "NaveenMandala", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/NaveenMandala", "username": "NaveenMandala", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e9/60/default-avatar-2020-64.jpg", "contribution_count": 11, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["